## 🏗️ Code Architecture Rules

### File Structure
```
app/                    # Expo Router pages (file-based routing)
├── (tabs)/            # Tab navigation screens
├── auth/              # Authentication screens
├── _layout.tsx        # Root layout
└── index.tsx          # Entry point

components/            # Reusable UI components
├── ui/                # Base UI components
└── ThemedText.tsx     # Themed components

stores/                # Zustand state stores
lib/                   # Utilities and configurations
├── supabase/         # Supabase client and types
└── secure-storage.ts  # Secure storage utilities

hooks/                 # Custom React hooks
utils/                 # Helper functions
constants/             # App constants
__tests__/             # Test files
```

### State Management
- Use **Zustand** for global state (auth, user data)
- Keep state stores in `stores/` directory
- Use local state (useState) for component-specific state
- Avoid prop drilling - use stores for shared state

### Authentication
- All auth logic in `stores/use-auth-store.ts`
- Use secure storage for session persistence
- Session validation happens on app initialization
- Protected routes use `Stack.Protected` with guard functions

