## 🔒 Security & Best Practices

### Authentication
- Never store sensitive data in plain text
- Use `expo-secure-store` for session tokens
- Validate session expiration on app initialization
- Clear secure storage on sign out

### Supabase
- Use Row Level Security (RLS) for database access
- Never expose service role keys in client code
- Use environment variables for Supabase credentials
- Client communicates directly with Supabase (no custom backend)

### Code Quality
- Remove console.log statements in production code
- Keep console.error for error handling
- Remove unused imports and dead code
- Follow ESLint rules (run `npm run lint`)

